<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Go-En'yū</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1359">1359</a>–1393</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Go-En'yū was the fifth emperor of the Northern Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, reigning from 1371 to 1382. A son of Go-Kōgon, he reigned during the ascendancy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshimitsu">Ashikaga Yoshimitsu</a>, who dominated the court. He abdicated in favour of his son Go-Komatsu and died in 1393, a year after the reunification of the Northern and Southern Courts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-go-enyu.jpg" alt="Emperor Go-En'yū" width="320" height="612" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tosa Mitsunobu (Inscription by the Emperor Go-Tsuchimikado) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Go-En%27y%C5%AB.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
